   "Author" or "Licensor" means Mark Jen (Jenerator Labs), the original author
   of beech, and his designated successors or assigns.

   "Software" means the beech source code, assets, shaders, scripts, server
   code, documentation, and related files distributed under this License.

   "Derivative Work" means any fork, modification, adaptation, translation,
   port, hosted service, mobile application, or other work based upon or
   incorporating all or any substantial portion of the Software.

   "You" or "Licensee" means any individual, company, or other legal entity
   exercising permissions granted by this License.

   "Host" means any server, instance, application, or service operated by You
   that hosts, stores, or serves player beaches using the Software or a
   Derivative Work.

   "Beechshore" means the public shore directory, discovery, and browsing
   service operated by the Licensor at https://beechshore.com (including any
   successor domain or federation network designated by the Licensor).

   "Public Beach" means any beach on a Host that its player has chosen to make
   public or place on the shore (as distinct from beaches explicitly kept
   private or off-shore by the player, or removed for moderation/safety).

   "Gross Revenue" means all money and monetary value collected, received, or
   earned by You (or by any affiliate, partner, or payment intermediary on Your
   behalf) arising from or connected to the Software or a Derivative Work. This
   includes, without limitation, in-app purchases, web checkout payments,
   virtual goods, subscriptions, access fees, sponsorships, advertising revenue,
   donations or tips tied to access or in-game benefits, white-label or
   sublicensing fees, and platform payouts. Gross Revenue is calculated before
   deducting hosting, infrastructure, development, marketing, support, or other
   operating expenses, and excludes only sales taxes, VAT, or similar
   transaction taxes actually collected from users and remitted to a taxing
   authority, and bona fide customer refunds or chargebacks actually returned.

2. Grant of Rights

   Subject to Your strict compliance with all conditions in this License, the
   Licensor hereby grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive, revocable (upon
   breach), royalty-bearing license to:

   (a) Copy, fork, study, modify, and create Derivative Works of the Software;
   (b) Build, distribute, and publish the Software and Derivative Works on web,
