   (c) Host and operate the Software and Derivative Works as a public or
       private service; and
   (d) Monetize and collect revenue from the Software and Derivative Works.

3. Condition 1 — 30% Gross Revenue Share

   (a) Revenue Share Obligation. If You collect any Gross Revenue from the
       Software or a Derivative Work, You must pay thirty percent (30%) of all
       Gross Revenue to the Licensor.

   (b) Zero-Revenue Use. If Your use generates no Gross Revenue, no payment is
       due under this Section.

   (c) Reporting and Payment Schedule. Within thirty (30) days after the end of
       each calendar quarter in which You collect Gross Revenue, You must:
       (i)  Send a clear revenue statement to the Licensor at markjen@gmail.com
            (or another reporting channel designated by the Licensor) detailing
            total Gross Revenue by source, applicable tax exclusions and
            refunds, and the 30% amount due; and
       (ii) Remit the full 30% payment in USD (or another currency agreed in
            writing by the Licensor) via a payment method designated by the
            Licensor.

   (d) No Circumvention. You may not structure pricing, bundles, affiliated
       entities, companion apps, or off-platform payments to avoid or reduce
       the Gross Revenue subject to this License.

   (e) Records and Verification. You must keep accurate books and records
       sufficient to verify Gross Revenue for at least three (3) years after
       each reporting period and provide reasonable supporting documentation
       (such as payment processor or app store payout statements) upon the
       Licensor's reasonable written request.

4. Condition 2 — Beechshore Interoperability and Federation

   A core purpose of beech is a shared, open shore across independent Hosts.
   If You operate a Host serving player beaches, You must ensure that Public
   Beaches on Your Host remain connectable, shareable, and browsable into
   Beechshore:

   (a) Connectable. Public Beaches on Your Host must be able to connect with
       beaches on Beechshore and on other compliant Hosts—including neighbor
       linking, direct visiting by code or URL, and cross-host shore adjacency
       as supported by the Software and Beechshore federation protocols.

   (b) Shareable. Share links, beach codes, previews, and beach exports for
       Public Beaches on Your Host must remain compatible with Beechshore and
       shareable into Beechshore without artificial technical barriers.

   (c) Browsable. Public Beaches on Your Host must be exposed for discovery,
       indexing, preview rendering, and browsing in Beechshore (for example,
       through the Software's public shore endpoints and any federation APIs
       published by the Licensor). You must not wall off Public Beaches behind
       anti-interoperability blocks, exclusive lock-in, or paywalls that
       prevent Beechshore from listing, previewing, or linking to them.

   (d) Player Privacy Respected. This requirement applies only to Public
       Beaches. Hosts must continue to respect a player's choice to keep a
       beach private / off-shore, as well as reasonable moderation, safety, and
       anti-abuse measures.

   (e) Protocol Updates. As the Licensor publishes or updates open federation
       and Beechshore integration specifications in the official repository,
       active Hosts must adopt and maintain reasonable compatibility within
       ninety (90) days of publication, unless granted a written extension or
       waiver by the Licensor.

